  "id": "risk-proneness",
  "term": "risk proneness",
  "definition": "Risk proneness is a tendency to favor an option with uncertain outcomes, especially when its possible gains are appealing. In this source, it refers to showing greater preference for risky choices, with that preference shifting depending on how the decision context presents risk.",
